# Declared Merlin-shaped instance for the TRAF-51 calibration comparison.
# Refined from the shipped UNVERIFIED placeholder
# (third_party/htsim: htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/ss_dragonfly/
# merlin_a100_5node_4x200g.topo at the pinned fabric merge) using the
# byte-locked capture dataset's discovery evidence
# (examples/merlin_fabric_flow_capture_v1/dataset, manifest SHA-256
# a6b7e61e294d87d76ce69ee7042e15c2eade99bbc8789e296377615d2bd4af88).
#
# Shape: the single-switch degenerate dragonfly p = 20, a = 1, h = 0,
# g = 1. Five-node socket-level discovery determines the per-port rate,
# the port count per node, and coarse pair latency; it cannot see beyond
# one switch, so the smallest consistent shape is all twenty 200G ports
# of the five A100 nodes (gpu101 to gpu105) on one Rosetta-class switch.
# Endpoint numbering: host = node * 4 + port, node 0..4 in hostname
# order gpu101..gpu105, port 0..3 in hsn order. Every parameter below
# carries its provenance tag: measured (from the dataset's evidence
# bytes), derived (arithmetic on measured values plus a stated public
# framing model), declared (chosen with a stated reason, not Merlin
# evidence).
#
# per-parameter provenance:
#   hosts_per_router 20, routers_per_group 1, global_links_per_router 0,
#     groups 1: declared-with-reason (smallest shape consistent with the
#     five-node discovery; the progressive adaptive routing machinery is
#     structurally unreachable at this shape and every delivery is
#     same-router).
#   host_link_gbps 200: measured (4 x Cray Cassini 1 SS11 200Gb 2P per
#     node in every guards_before/after port inventory of the dataset).
#   host_link_latency_ps 300000: declared-with-reason (physical
#     propagation plus NIC serdes order for machine-room copper; the
#     socket-level 8-byte one-way measurements, 18.98 to 25.60 us, are
#     host-stack-dominated and only bound this term from above; at 8 MiB
#     chunks the term is 0.09 percent of the fabric chunk time, so the
#     calibration is insensitive to it; kept at the fixture default).
#   switch_pipeline_ps 350000: declared-from-published-measurement (the
#     350 ns mean Rosetta latency of De Sensi et al., SC'20, II-A; not
#     measured on Merlin).
#   rosetta_buffer_bytes 4194304: declared (Rosetta buffer sizing is
#     unpublished; fixture default; solo-cell occupancy stays at the
#     in-service packet scale, so the scored cells are insensitive).
#   max_wire_packet_bytes 9038: derived (measured MTU 9000 on every hsn
#     interface; TCP MSS 8948 at IPv4 plus TCP timestamps; Ethernet
#     framing plus FCS, preamble and IFG give 9038 wire bytes per
#     packet; the dataset's sender-side tx counter overhead of 0.64
#     percent over payload is consistent with this framing family to
#     within 0.2 percent). The harness overrides this knob per
#     invocation; every scored invocation passes -wire_bytes 9038
#     -header_bytes 90 so payload per packet is 8948 bytes.
#   routing_seed 383530136519245852: declared (determinism identity,
#     fixture default; routing is degenerate at this shape).
#   congestion quantizers and advertisement cadence: left at the fabric
#     header defaults; structurally unreachable at a single switch (no
#     inter-switch links exist to advertise over).
#
# Status: declared instance for the calibration study; not a claim about
# the site-wide Merlin dragonfly shape beyond what five nodes determine.
topology dragonfly
hosts_per_router 20
routers_per_group 1
global_links_per_router 0
groups 1
host_link_gbps 200
host_link_latency_ps 300000
switch_pipeline_ps 350000
rosetta_buffer_bytes 4194304
max_wire_packet_bytes 9038
routing_seed 383530136519245852
